+In rounded arithmetic, accept a candidate only when a validated upper enclosure proves the displayed inequality. Obtain the backend's validated upper bound $U\ge mG_K(\mu)$ as required by the input contract, and set the returned certificate $T:=\varepsilon$ by copying the supplied budget; the accepted comparison certifies $mG_K(\mu)\le T$. No comparison or sharper enclosure of $U$ is required. If no candidate works, return `budget-exhausted` when the comparisons certify that every candidate fails, and `certificate-unavailable` when they do not decide the search. In exact arithmetic set $T=mG_K(\mu)$. Set $P=I+Q/\nu$ and $x_0=p_0$. For each substep $j=1,\ldots,m$, initialize $v_0=x_{j-1}$, $w_0=e^{-\mu}$, and $x_j=w_0v_0$. For $k=0,\ldots,K-1$, update
 
 $$v_{k+1}=Pv_k,\qquad w_{k+1}=w_k\frac{\mu}{k+1},\qquad x_j\leftarrow x_j+w_{k+1}v_{k+1}.$$
 
